ombat or in post-fight activities**\n- **Actively engaged in combat.** All frames from 2505 to 2533 show continuous grappling — Royce Gracie in top position, applying pressure, while Ken Shamrock is defending on the bottom.\n- No post-fight handshakes, celebrations, or referee interventions signaling the end are visible.\n\n---\n\n### 6. **Round transitions or time announcements**\n- No round transition is visible.\n- The timer is counting up within a single round (4:05 to 4:33), not resetting or indicating a new round.\n- No audible or visual round bell or announcement is present in these frames.\n\n---\n\n### Conclusion: Does “2” (36 minutes) match the visual evidence?\n\n- **No.**\n- The provided frames cover only **a 28-second segment** of active grappling, occurring around the **4:05–4:33 mark of a round**.\n- There is **no visual evidence** to support a total match duration of 36 minutes.\n- In fact, **UFC V’s Shamrock vs. Gracie fight ended at 15:00 of the first round via referee stoppage due to exhaustion**, not 36 minutes. (Historical context: This was a 15-minute round with no time limit, but it ended at 15:00 due to Gracie’s exhaustion, not a 36-minute duration.)\n\n---\n\n### Final Answer:\n**The visual evidence in these frames does not support a match duration of 36 minutes. The answer “2” is incorrect based on the provided frames.** The frames show only a brief segment of grappling within a single round, not the full match duration.'}, {'batch_start': 60, 'batch_end': 90, 'image_paths': ['/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/cXDT44zT8JY/frames/frame_2534.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/cXDT44zT8JY/frames/frame_2535.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/cXDT44zT8JY/frames/frame_2536.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/cXDT44zT8JY/frames/frame_2537.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/cXDT44zT8JY/frames/frame_2538.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/cXDT44zT8JY/frames/frame_2539.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lv